{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>But on the fifteenth day, etc.</b> Rashi explained: I might think the festal offering could push off the Sabbath — Scripture says: 'אַךְ (only).' And the difficulty is: who even mentioned Sabbath? Rather, it appears that this is its meaning: 'But on the fifteenth day of the month, when you gather the produce of the land' — that is, on a day when it is permitted to gather the produce from the field, at the very least for the need of food for the soul, which is on a Festival day that does not fall on the Sabbath — on that day you shall celebrate the festal offering; but not on a day when there is no gathering from the field in any respect at all, even if one has nothing to eat — and that is the Sabbath. For had 'אַךְ' not been said, I would have said that 'when you gather' refers to the season of gathering, and not to a day on which there is gathering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:38:13.460410011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}